    "explicit_thread_index_kernel": {
      "median_us": 3.97,
      "ratio": 0.97,
      "rejected_reason": "not host-portable: the host OpenMP executor (OmpBlocks) requires one thread per block and produces wrong results with an exact multi-thread ThreadSpec"
    },
    "ncu_kernel_time_us": {
      "alpaka": 6.7,
      "reference": 5.4
    },
    "decision": "keep the portable single-source makeIdxMap form; accept the ~11% documented exception"
  },
  "cpu_reference_note": "The HeCBench affine-omp source uses an OpenMP target offload region that g++ cannot compile and icpx/nvc are absent, so the CPU baseline is the same source with the offload pragmas replaced by a plain host parallel-for (14 threads), median 272.7 us over 7 runs of 2000 iters."
